  "seed_id": "5fd515f1d6a6f6a8",
  "prompt": "You are an associate analyst on the Halverson Stuyvesant consumer sector team. Rashida Holm, the managing director, has asked you to prepare a quarter-over-quarter margin variance analysis on NIKE, Inc. (NKE) ahead of an internal investment committee discussion on the company's margin trajectory. Your analysis will be based on the latest 10-Q and the attached historical financial summary (NKE_historical_financials.xlsx).\n\nPull the three-month period ended figures for the quarter ending February 28, 2026. The pinned P&L data: Revenue of $35.426B, COGS of $20.908B, Gross Profit of $14.518B, SGA of $12.032B, and Net Income of $2.039B. Diluted EPS was $1.38. Total Assets stood at $37.064B, Stockholders' Equity at $14.09B, and Cash at $6.66B.\n\nBuild the deliverable as an Excel workbook with the following structure:\n\n1. Calculate gross margin, operating margin (Gross Profit less SGA), and net margin for Q3 FY2026 (three months ended 2/28/2026) using the figures above. Express all margins as percentages and to two decimal places.\n\n2. Source the corresponding three-month period figures for the immediately prior sequential quarter from the most recent prior 10-Q on EDGAR and compute the same three margins. Use only the quarterly column, not YTD.\n\n3. Compute the quarter-over-quarter basis-point change for gross margin, operating margin, and net margin. Present all margin deltas in basis points — institutional audience.\n\n4. Decompose the gross margin variance into volume/mix, price, and cost components to the extent the filing's MD&A and footnotes allow. If disclosures are insufficient for clean separation, note what's available and what isn't.\n\n5. Attribute the operating margin variance between gross profit flow-through and SGA leverage (SGA as a % of revenue). Show the mechanical bridge.\n\n6. Build a waterfall-style variance bridge tab showing the QoQ change in each margin line item from gross margin through net margin, with intermediate operating margin waterfall.\n\n7. Flag any one-time or non-recurring items disclosed in the filing that materially affected the margin comparison (restructuring, impairment, tax items, etc.).\n\n8. Include a 2-3 sentence qualitative commentary section summarizing the primary margin drivers for the quarter.\n\nFormat notes: follow Halverson Stuyvesant template conventions — header row formatting, color coding distinguishing inputs from formulas, consistent number formatting. Negative variances in parentheses, not minus signs. All EDGAR-sourced figures must reconcile to the original filing with no unannotated manual adjustments. This will be presented to the investment committee with minimal further review.",
  "deliverable": {
    "deliverable_id": "variance_analysis",
    "primary_format": "xlsx",
    "expected_size": null
  },
